From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:32:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 29/35] PROTOTYPE pco: commute fadd/fmul/fmad sources instead
 of copying a shared register

Shared and coefficient registers can only be read through S0, S2 and S3.
A uniform in the second source of fadd/fmul/fmad (S1) was copied into a
temp by a mov group of its own, once per use, per pixel. The first two
sources commute: when the swap makes both readable, swap them instead.
Only without source modifiers, whose support differs between the slots.
Chromium's YUV shader (Angelfish) copied a matrix uniform before nearly
every fmad.

Generated-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit e3dc3d78915e113e3a99a20f4302110f21865c9c)
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_legalize.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_legalize.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_legalize.c
index 456e528a183..a2d2fc8cc0b 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_legalize.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_legalize.c
@@ -99,6 +99,28 @@ static bool try_legalize_src_mappings(pco_instr *instr,
    bool progress = false;
    bool needs_s124;
 
+   /* fadd/fmul/fmad (first two sources) commute: if the second source can't
+    * be read through its slot (a shared or coefficient register in S1) but
+    * the first can take its place and vice versa, swap them rather than
+    * copying the register into a temp with a mov of its own.
+    */
+   if ((instr->op == PCO_OP_FADD || instr->op == PCO_OP_FMUL ||
+        instr->op == PCO_OP_FMAD) &&
+       info->src_intrn_map[0] && info->src_intrn_map[1] &&
+       !pco_ref_has_mods_set(instr->src[0]) &&
+       !pco_ref_has_mods_set(instr->src[1])) {
+      enum pco_io io0 = PCO_IO_S0 + info->src_intrn_map[0] - 1;
+      enum pco_io io1 = PCO_IO_S0 + info->src_intrn_map[1] - 1;
+
+      if (!ref_src_map_valid(instr->src[1], io1, NULL) &&
+          ref_src_map_valid(instr->src[1], io0, NULL) &&
+          ref_src_map_valid(instr->src[0], io1, NULL)) {
+         pco_ref tmp = instr->src[0];
+         instr->src[0] = instr->src[1];
+         instr->src[1] = tmp;
+      }
+   }
+
    /* Check dests. */
    pco_foreach_instr_dest (pdest, instr) {
       unsigned dest_index = pdest - instr->dest;
